<div class="bb-quote"><b>sandgoblin18 wrote:</b><br /><blockquote class="bb-quote-body">I&#39;m telling you guys, quite possible the best team I have ever played with is Legacy, Tachyon, Guise, and Captain Cosmic. &nbsp;Start with Completionist Guise for it to work, and also start with Team Leader Tachyon and Green CC to start for best effect. Those two are absolutely two of teh best heroes in the game. &nbsp;For Legacy, start with whatever floats your boat/is best for the matchup.First, after CC gets some constructs up, you can sub in XPW CC and start hammering away. &nbsp;Who says CC doesn&#39;t deal damage? &nbsp;Also, a note; even without Completionist Guise, green CC is good. &nbsp;Like, really good. &nbsp;CC can destroy his own constructs with most of his one shots, making the negative part happen less often than you might think.Play the game as you would, jumping around with Legacy so Guise can use the powers, and also for green CC is the constructs get culled, up until Tachyon has managed to get a lot of burst in and hopefully played a lightspeed or two. &nbsp;Then, sub out for regular legacy, galvanize, blitz. &nbsp;A friend and I did this combo, and we have a house rule that the game doesn&#39;t end until the end of the last hero turn once the villain dies, so we can deal overkill damage just for fun. &nbsp;With this combo, we ended up dealing 137 damage to Infinitor. &nbsp;That&#39;s double his life, so as you may notice, more than half of that came in the final round. &nbsp;We kind of cheated, in that we specifically left him with 4 life the round before, but hey, fun&#39;s fun! &nbsp;&nbsp;
&nbsp;
</blockquote></div>
&nbsp;

For a fifth, argent would be silly.

[/quote]

I was thinking Visionary. Enlighten to help get bursts into the trash. Twist the Ether for boosted Blitzes of any type. Plus Crushing Lucidity from Unleashed Visionary for that little bit of extra damage if you&#39;re feeling hurty.

